{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Capture a page as a PNG. Two modes. LIVE (url empty): captures the DRIVEN tab's actual pixels - its real current DOM, mutations, and login state - by sending a chrome-targeted request (//NOOBSCAPE-CHROME) that a parent-process chrome docshell answers with drawSnapshot on the bound browsing context (bind.id), encoding via OffscreenCanvas and writing with IOUtils; errs when no session is running. Each async step is bounded by an internal timeout and the driver retries up to 3x, so an occasional headless drawSnapshot stall recovers (result carries attempts). URL (url non-empty): shoots that URL via Firefox's own --headless --screenshot against a throwaway profile - a fresh anonymous load, so logged-out. path empty defaults to runtime/agent/screenshots/shot-<millis>.png; width/height <=0 default 1280x1024 (in live mode this is the top-left rect captured at scale 1). Returns {status, mode(live|url), path (absolute), bytes, url, width, height, attempts?}.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse flowlang::rand::rand_range;\nuse std::process::Command;","params":[{"desc":"Page to capture. Empty string means the LIVE driven tab's actual pixels (its real DOM, mutations, and login state) via drawSnapshot on the bound browsing context; errs when empty and no session is running. A non-empty URL takes the throwaway-profile CLI path (fresh anonymous load, logged-out).","name":"url","type":"String"},{"desc":"Output PNG path. Empty string defaults to runtime/agent/screenshots/shot-<millis>.png. Relative paths resolve against the instance root.","name":"path","type":"String"},{"desc":"Capture width in px; <=0 defaults to 1280. In live mode this is the top-left rect of the document captured at scale 1.","name":"width","type":"Integer"},{"desc":"Capture height in px; <=0 defaults to 1024.","name":"height","type":"Integer"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"rvuzgy1a03fb16529n1","readers":[],"time":1788622810898,"username":"system","writers":[]}